 - **Steps.** Model steps: `z-ticket`, `z-design`, `z-raft`, `z-run` and `zz-review` (modes `design`, `raft`, `code`, `stream`). Script steps, which the dispatcher runs itself and never starts a model for: `z-ready` (`./zn ready`), `z-stop` (`./zn stop`), `raft-plan --apply`, `recombine`, `fold`, `release`, `spend` and `zz-stats` (`./zn metrics`). `zz-rules`, `zz-arch`, `zz-test`, `zz-execute` (the protocol z-work follows) and a project's skills are read inside a step and are never one. `z-work` is a person's session and is never a dispatch step. Any other name is an error.
-- **`.models.toml`.** At the repository root, and optionally closer to the work (a project's home, an issue's folder). It stacks like `.gitignore`: a closer file replaces only the keys it sets (each `[dispatch]` setting, each field of each `[roles.<name>]`, each field of each `[fallback.<cli>]`). the supported CLIs are `claude`, `grok` and `agent` (Cursor), and `kimi`, and a table naming any other is an error. A role has `model`, `cli`, `runtime`, `rank` and `max_tokens` (and optionally `effort` and `fallbacks`), and an `agent` role or fallback also `max_calls` and `max_minutes`: Cursor's `agent` reports no running token count, so its step stops after `max_calls` model calls (distinct `model_call_id`s, and each turn that carries none) and the spend row takes the result's real total; a stream with three turns in a row and no `model_call_id`, or a line it doesn't know, stops as `cap-unknown` (fail closed); calls are not tokens, so the user tunes it, and an `agent` role or fallback without it is an error, never unlimited (the user's "Cap model calls, record real total"); a call count can miss calls, so the step also stops (`cap`) after `max_minutes` of wall time; the runtime belongs to its CLI: `claude-cli`, `grok-cli` and `cursor-cli`, and `kimi-cli` (the remote runtimes are c0142's). Nothing defaults: a role no file names, a missing field, or no file at all is an error naming it. A step about one issue walks to that issue's folder; a step about a raft walks to each member's and takes, per CLI, the stronger spec whole (higher `rank`, then larger `max_tokens`), in the raft's own walk's try list; z-ticket walks to the project's home. The `[dispatch]` settings (`auto_merge`, `stall_seconds`, `tool_seconds`) come from the item's own walk; an unset or unreadable `auto_merge` is none. Every file is read as committed on `main` (fetched once per run), never from the working tree: an uncommitted `.models.toml` on the walk is an error, so a new one takes effect once its PR has